"$1d\\\",\\\"$1e\\\",\\\"$29\\\"],\\\"$2a\\\"]\\n2c:T429,\\u003cp\\u003eType once. Cuey fans the prompt out to the major models and returns the answers in one clean comparison view. No tab juggling and no subscription Tetris — the same question answered several ways with the differences impossible to miss.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u003eWhy comparing models is now a real workflow\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eThe model market has stopped being a one-horse race. Writing quality and reasoning depth and code accuracy all drift apart across providers — and the gap is task-specific rather than general. Experienced users already behave this way by hand. Cuey simply removes the friction of doing it manually.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eA quiet pricing lesson\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eSeeing answers side by side also makes subscription stacking visible. Most people do not need three premium plans — they need one good default plus a comparison habit for the few tasks where the choice actually matters.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eMy own rule after months of daily model use: pick the model per task instead of per brand. The \\u003ca href=\\\"/services\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\"\\u003eidea-to-product pipeline\\u003c/a\\u003e I run works exactly the same way.\\u003c/p\\u003e25:[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"script\\\",null,{\\\"type\\\":\\\"application/ld+json\\\",\\\"suppressHydrationWarning\\\":true,\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"@context\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://schema.org\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"@type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Article\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"headline\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cuey compares ChatGPT and Claude and Gemini in a single tab\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"alternativeHeadline\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cuey — مقایسهٔ ChatGPT و Claude و Gemini در یک تب\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cuey sends one prompt to the leading AI models and lines the answers up side by side. It turns the hunch every power user already has — that models are good at different things — in